{
  "_about": {
    "what": "What regions_report.py asserts, keyed by Postman item name. Keys starting with an underscore are ignored.",
    "shape": "{ \"<item name>\": { \"verdict\": \"PASS\"|null, \"http_status\": 400, \"criteria\": { \"<criterion>\": {\"status\": \"ok\"|\"skipped\"|\"error\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\"|null, \"min_regions\": 1, \"item_verdicts\": [\"FAIL\", \"PASS\"], \"region_pages\": [0, 1]} } } }",
    "verdict_null": "A criterion with \"verdict\": null asserts NOTHING about the verdict. Every `llm` row is written that way on purpose: its score comes from a model, and a suite that claims to verify a model's judgement against a fixed answer is lying about what it measured.",
    "min_regions": "Asserted for the deterministic paths (cv / ocr / pdf-text) where the fixtures' READMEs document a count. For `options.boxes` rows it is 0 — 'you may produce boxes, and if you do they will be drawn' — so nothing false is claimed either way.",
    "http_status": "When present, the item is expected to be REJECTED at submit time and nothing else is asserted.",
    "sources": [
      "unit-tests/classifier/documents/README.md",
      "unit-tests/classifier/regions/README.md",
      "ai/classifier/API.md"
    ],
    "adding_a_case": "Add the Postman item, then an entry here. See unit-tests/classifier/REGIONS_REPORT.md.",
    "status": "A criterion that is not evaluated has `status: \"skipped\"` and a null verdict (it used to be `verdict: \"SKIPPED\"`), so skipped rows assert the status instead. A `score: false` criterion has a null verdict by design.",
    "local_mode": "Under --local, `llm` and `detector` criteria are dropped; a criterion that still reaches the model (a cv name with no OpenCV detector falls back to the llm) comes back status: error, and its checks and the overall verdict are recorded as skipped.",
    "per_item": "A request may carry several documents, and every page is one item. \"item_verdicts\" asserts the criterion's per-unit answers in order (one per item — one per document for a text criterion with options.scope \"document\"): a verdict, or \"skipped\" / \"error\" for a unit that did not answer; null asserts nothing. \"region_pages\" is the sorted set of items its regions landed on. The criterion's own \"verdict\" is the AGGREGATED answer."
  },
